From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: add acs_scan_duration option for ACS scan dwell

Add acs_scan_duration (0..1000 ms, default 0) to hostapd configuration.
When set to 0, behaviour is unchanged. Otherwise acs_request_scan()
converts the value to TUs with rounding (e.g. 300 ms -> 293 TU) and sets
params.duration with duration_mandatory=0 and a new duration_advisory
bit in struct wpa_driver_scan_params.

nl80211_scan_common() checks WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_SUPPORT_SET_SCAN_DWELL
before sending NL80211_ATTR_MEASUREMENT_DURATION, and mac80211 software
scan drivers (such as mt7603e, mt76x2e, and mac80211_hwsim) do not
advertise NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_SET_SCAN_DWELL even though mac80211
honours scan_req->duration. Allow nl80211_scan_common() to send
NL80211_ATTR_MEASUREMENT_DURATION when duration_advisory is set and
duration_mandatory is off, leaving all other callers unchanged.

Note on units: NL80211_ATTR_MEASUREMENT_DURATION is defined in TUs
(1.024 ms), which hardware-scan drivers honouring the attribute read as
TUs, whereas mac80211 software scan passes scan_req->duration directly to
msecs_to_jiffies() as a minimum dwell (at HZ=100, below 110 ms stays
110 ms, and 300 ms -> 293 TU -> 30 jiffies = 300 ms).
---
 hostapd/config_file.c             |  8 ++++++++
 hostapd/hostapd.conf              |  9 +++++++++
 src/ap/acs.c                      | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/ap/ap_config.c                |  1 +
 src/ap/ap_config.h                |  1 +
 src/drivers/driver.h              |  8 ++++++++
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211_scan.c |  5 +++--
 wpa_supplicant/scan.c             |  1 +
 8 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

